WEBVTT

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:14.260
"Hachiko"

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.680
"0 months, 7 days"

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:17.930
"0 months, 7 days"
My second game's started.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:28.940
This isn't the end.
We'll win and come back to life.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:35.030
When we come back to life,
I want all of us to meet up again.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.580
You can recognize me by Mr. Mew.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:40.790
OK.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.080
Sorry I'm late!

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.290
Shiki--

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:49.000
Clothes shopping, right? Where to?

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.420
How about Modi and Parco?

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.170
Wanna swing by Tokyu Hands?

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:54.470
--Sure! Let's go.

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:56.510
--Shiki should've been like them.
--Sure! Let's go.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:01.060
But I...

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.390
Neku...

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:15.610
If I survive these seven days,
Shiki will come back.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.080
"The World Ends With You The Animation"

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.960
"#04: Reapers"

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.130
A mission?

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:54.170
Listen up, Players!

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:55.250
What?!

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.380
You're all pawns!

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:59.470
Do what I tell you!

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:00.340
Game one!

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:04.430
Calculate the square root of 10,816

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:06.970
and seek out the solution!

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:09.020
You have 60 minutes!

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:11.770
I'll only spare the ones who show up!

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:15.230
Incompletes get destroyed!
Destroyed! Destroyed!

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.650
It's a lot different from last time.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.410
We beat Higashizawa.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:24.070
So, was that the new Game Master?

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:29.450
These are nothing!

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.580
I can't use psychs?!

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.050
Struggling your second time around?

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:47.680
All right,

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.350
I'll be your partner.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:58.690
I can fight!

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:16.080
I knew you could do it, Neku.

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:23.680
I've been watching you for a long time.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:27.600
The way you fought was wonderful.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.260
You were?

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:31.310
I don't know you.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.310
I'm Yoshiya Kiryu.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.860
Please, call me Joshua.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.650
Was he a Player in the last game?

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:44.610
No. He wasn't one of the survivors.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.370
Don't look so intimidating.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:50.240
It's day one, so let's take it easy.

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:52.580
Hey!

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:57.880
Enjoy every moment.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:03.470
What was that?

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.630
Did I scan him?

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:07.340
What's wrong?

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:11.520
No, Players aren't supposed
to be able to scan each other.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:16.980
That's not good. I need you to escort me.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:20.980
You'll never win if you
don't trust your partner.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:24.780
I can't trust this guy yet.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:27.360
But the mission's already started.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.410
I'll team up with you.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:35.160
I think we'll make a great team.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.960
Now, let's get going to 104.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.500
What for?

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.550
Couldn't solve the mission?

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:48.640
The square root of 10,816 is 104.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.930
Meaning that's where we should go.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.140
Come on.

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:06.700
Has the game ever run two
weeks in a row before?

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.780
Yeah, once, a long time ago.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:12.330
A rookie like you wouldn't know, Uzuki.

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:15.370
"Rookie"? This is my second year.

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:18.790
How long have you been a Reaper?

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:21.920
Don't sweat the small stuff.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:25.670
For now, all we've got
to do is stand around.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:28.630
This is why I hate working under that guy.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:31.220
I can't score any points.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:36.430
I bet he's got some crazy plan that'd
go right over our ordinary heads.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.060
I mean, he's the solitary genius
who made that thing.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:41.900
"104"

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.110
What's this thing?

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:45.320
Is that "guerilla art"?

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:49.610
Wh-What the...?!

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:52.450
This junk wasn't here last time.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:53.870
Someone's here.

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:01.580
Zetta slow!

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.210
You're zetta slow!

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:07.130
How long did it take you to crack
that code, you hectopascals?!

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:08.880
H-Hecto... what?

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:11.680
Does this mean we've cleared the mission?

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.600
Oh, you're right.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:20.940
I'm Sho Minamimoto,
your Game Master this time around!

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:25.270
Putting in an appearance on day one?
How unconventional of you.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:27.360
Convention is trash!

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:28.940
Crush!

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:31.110
On the scrap heap it goes!

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:32.320
Hmm?

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:37.910
You're a Player this time?

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:40.040
You recognize me?

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:44.630
A happy miscalculation.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:47.710
This brings me closer
to my desired solution.

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:49.010
"Solution"?

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:50.670
What do you mean?

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:56.850
The games I design require
flawless calculations...

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.350
...and beauty!

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:00.930
I see the rumors were true.

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:04.100
Some Old Horses Can Always
Hear Their Owner Approach.

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:08.440
Listen up!

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:13.450
The weight I'm gonna let you
Players carry in the Underground...

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.780
...is 1 yoctogram!

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:17.780
Would that be at the atomic level?

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:19.620
I'm totally lost.

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:26.380
No dice. It didn't open either.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:31.130
So, Route 4 is open,
and 1 and 2 are sealed.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:35.140
Routes 5 and 6 are sealed too, right?

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:39.100
Told you he's a genius. He works fast.

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:42.560
He didn't even let us know
what areas are open.

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:45.270
Doesn't he care about us
Reapers on the ground?

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:47.230
I can't stand him.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:49.230
What's the big deal?

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:53.530
Let's take a good look
at what the boss can do.

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:55.910
Isn't getting here enough to clear it?!

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:58.370
Weren't you going to spare us?!

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:00.160
--What do we have to do now?
--Is there another mission?

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:01.700
--I just wanna live again.
--Is there another mission?

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:02.870
Those guys...

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:04.540
"Man and woman in late teens
caught in accident, unconscious"

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.460
"Man and woman in late teens
caught in accident, unconscious"
Don't tell me...

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:07.080
"Man and woman in late teens
caught in accident, unconscious"
All you worthless little yoctograms!

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:11.710
I want all of you...

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:13.420
...to die here!

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:40.780
Listen up! I just added a new mission!

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:43.370
Player vs. Player. To the death.

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:45.710
I'll save the winners.

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:58.640
Don't listen to that Reaper!

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:00.390
Trust your partners!

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:04.810
If you don't work together,
you'll get erased!

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:19.820
That was a close one.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.790
Its weak point is its back.

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:29.540
Hear that?! We've gotta fight too!

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:33.840
Wh-What the hell?!

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:36.260
I-I don't want to die.

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:39.640
S-Stop! Calm down!

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:42.680
Good work!

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.100
Next,

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:47.230
I'll save whoever takes down that Reaper.

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:48.440
What?!

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:54.820
Come and...

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:58.110
...get it!

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:09.710
This is our chance.

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:13.590
Let's show them what we can do.

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:16.420
Come on, Neku.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:17.880
Try asking first.

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:28.930
Is this to your liking?

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:05.220
What is this power?

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:08.810
It looks like we really
do make a good team.

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.850
This will make all seven days a cakewalk.

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:16.900
As long as you and I keep up
our wonderful teamwork, that is.

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:21.070
I still barely know you.

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:27.030
But if you want to survive
any more Reapers' Games,

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:30.410
you'll have to trust me, Neku.

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:37.790
It looks like this game
is gonna be zetta fun!

00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:44.220
Don't you think so too?

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:52.060
Hi there. It's me.

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:57.650
In front of Hachiko again?

00:12:59.020 --> 00:12:59.690
"0 months, 6 days"

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:02.030
"0 months, 6 days"
The whole area's sealed?

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:04.820
Hmm. I see.

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:07.070
Who's he talking to?

00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:10.290
Then, if the wall on Route 3 opens,

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:13.620
I might be able to slip under
the guard in Miyashita Park.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:14.960
--Route 3? Miyashita Park?

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:16.920
--That's fine.
--Route 3? Miyashita Park?

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:19.290
Is he gonna swing by Cat Street?

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:22.880
I remember now!

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:26.510
I know Shibuya!

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:32.390
I know where I am and
the connecting streets.

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:38.060
Until a little while ago, I didn't
even know I was in Shibuya.

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:39.980
So, why now?

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:41.860
Of course!

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:44.360
When you enter the Reapers' Game,

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:49.200
they take whatever is most
important to you. No exceptions.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:54.040
Remember yesterday, when Rhyme said
she didn't know what dreams are?

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:58.670
I bet that was because it
was taken as her entry fee.

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:02.800
Just like how I can't remember anything.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:04.380
It came back!

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:06.470
My first entry fee!

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:10.680
My memories from when I was alive!

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.220
Enjoy every moment.

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:15.850
To do that with all I've got,

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:18.770
I'll do what I want, how I want,
as much as I want.

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:24.150
That graffiti is from Udagawa!

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:26.280
I saw it when I scanned him.

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:31.580
And he's supposed to be a Player,
so how'd I scan him at all?

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:34.370
Call me when it's ready. Later.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:39.330
What's wrong? You're looking grim.

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:41.290
None of your business.

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:47.760
Your last partner? That was a shame.

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:51.300
Hey... how much do you know?

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:52.720
It happens all the time.

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:56.350
Every Player has something
dear to them on the line.

00:14:58.100 --> 00:14:58.940
"Game II: Go to √3. You have 300 minutes.
Incompletes will be destroyed."

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:00.650
"Game II: Go to √3. You have 300 minutes.
Incompletes will be destroyed."
"Square root of 3."

00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:01.860
"Game II: Go to √3. You have 300 minutes.
Incompletes will be destroyed."
"Root 3."

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:04.360
Can you figure this one out?

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:06.070
What?

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:09.070
Route 3. You mentioned it on the phone.

00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:17.290
The Reapers refer to the streets
of Shibuya by numbers.

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:21.540
Route 1, Route 2, etc. in each area.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:23.130
You know a lot.

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:26.210
Let me give you a tip.

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:29.800
This is a Reaper decal.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:31.640
A Reaper what?

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:35.680
They're pasted on stores where
the Reapers allow us to shop.

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:36.640
Shop?

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:37.850
Hang on.

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:43.060
How'd you buy that?

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:46.780
I thought people in the
Realground couldn't see us.

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:47.990
Not normally.

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:49.030
Here.

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:54.530
We're made corporeal inside stores
with Reaper decals on them.

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:55.990
Why?

00:15:55.990 --> 00:16:00.710
Who knows. It seems like Reapers
can become corporeal at will.

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:05.090
What a shame. The Route 2 wall is sealed.

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:14.300
Skater-Brain.

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:15.760
Something wrong?

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:17.430
No, it's nothing.

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:19.980
Take us to Route 3.

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:22.190
This is Route 3.

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:25.400
It's the street that cuts
through from Modi to Parco.

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:30.530
The countdown's still going.

00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:34.620
Let's try walking.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:41.500
There's one here too?

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:52.420
Noise?

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:54.680
They seem different from usual.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:03.690
As if!

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:10.820
My attacks don't work?!

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:26.670
Thank you, Neku.

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:28.590
Let's do this together.

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:31.260
Fine.

00:17:35.300 --> 00:17:36.970
Focus.

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:38.850
Sharpen your senses.

00:17:54.780 --> 00:17:55.990
I can do this!

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:57.820
One more!

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:00.450
Chew on this!

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:12.170
What was that black Noise just now?

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:17.090
It seemed as though we could only
damage it by attacking together.

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:19.260
Oh, was that it?

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:21.720
Don't tell me you didn't realize.

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:24.140
As your partner, that's concerning.

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:26.480
There weren't any like that before.

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:32.610
Yes. It's odd.

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:34.400
Taboo Noise?

00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:36.740
You say something?

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:38.660
Nothing at all.

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:41.120
It seems like that cleared the mission.

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:47.210
That girl.

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:48.420
She's Shiki's...

00:18:57.550 --> 00:18:59.300
You always buy these.

00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:02.850
My friend liked them.

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:06.230
I don't want her to be lonely,
so every day I go to visit--

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:12.150
I mean, leave offerings for her.

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:14.820
Oh, wait a moment.

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:22.820
I'm the one who's lonely.

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:25.660
Sorry.

00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:29.410
It's my fault.

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:35.840
Shiki... I miss you.

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:38.670
Please, take this.

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:40.050
Huh?

00:19:40.050 --> 00:19:43.720
I put it in the back because
the flowers finished blooming,

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:46.350
but it's still pretty, so take it.

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:49.140
Thank you so much.

00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:51.230
Isn't that nice, Shiki?

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:04.530
She's skillful, sensitive,
and a hard worker.

00:20:04.530 --> 00:20:06.410
But now...

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:08.040
It's still...

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:10.750
...our dream.

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:14.710
I'll come back to life and
make clothes with her!

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:16.340
Do I...?

00:20:28.970 --> 00:20:31.560
When did I die?

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.650
Where? How?

00:20:34.860 --> 00:20:37.020
The memories I lost are coming back.

00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:39.610
But... I don't remember my death.

00:20:39.610 --> 00:20:40.860
Neku.

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:46.620
If you want to live,
you'd better listen to me.

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:49.620
I knew it! You do know something!

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:58.210
Why... am I lying there?

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:03.970
That's... Udagawa.

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:09.470
Blood.

00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:11.770
Is this my death?

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:14.810
Is Udagawa where...

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:16.400
...I died?

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:20.360
Neku?

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:25.490
Did you scan me, by any chance?

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:39.630
Beat?!

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:41.000
Hey...

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:43.260
...those wings!

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:45.760
You his new partner?

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:47.680
Yes, I am.

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:48.800
Who cares.

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:51.770
This order came straight from Kitaniji.

00:21:51.770 --> 00:21:53.980
I'll wipe the floor with you!

00:21:59.190 --> 00:22:00.440
You're weak!

00:22:01.530 --> 00:22:05.400
You think you'll stand
a chance like that?!

00:22:05.400 --> 00:22:07.200
Beat.

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:10.450
Shiki was taken as my entry fee.

00:22:10.450 --> 00:22:12.580
So...

00:22:12.580 --> 00:22:15.620
...I want to bring Shiki back to life!

00:22:15.620 --> 00:22:17.710
You wanted Rhyme to...

00:22:17.710 --> 00:22:20.210
I'll call it here for today.

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:23.920
Wait, Beat!

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:27.090
Beat!

00:23:59.480 --> 00:24:01.310
Next time: "CAT."
